{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U8", "U4"],
      "pins": ["U8.2", "U8.4", "U4.3"],
      "nets": ["I2C_SDA", "Net-(U8-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "U8 is a 74LVC1G34 single non-inverting buffer inserted in series with the EC isolator's SDA line. U4 pin 3 (SDA_2) connects only to U8 pin 2 (input), while U8 pin 4 (output) drives the main I2C_SDA net. U3's SDA_2 pin is connected directly to I2C_SDA.",
      "expected": "The primary-side SDA pin of each ADM3260 isolator (U3 and U4) should connect directly to the main bidirectional I2C_SDA bus, as specified for the primary side of U3/U4 bridging to the isolated pH/EC domains. I2C SDA is bidirectional and open-drain; a unidirectional buffer cannot be placed in series without breaking bidirectional communication.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"78\") (name \"I2C_SDA\") ... (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"4\") (pintype \"output\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"119\") (name \"Net-(U8-Pad2)\") (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"SDA_{2}\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"input\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Primary (non-isolated) side of U3 and U4 (ADM3260 isolators), which bridge through to the isolated pH/EC domains."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(libsource (lib \"74xGxx\") (part \"74LVC1G34\") (description \"Single Buffer Gate, Low-Voltage CMOS\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The EC I2C channel is broken: the ESP32/main bus cannot drive U4's SDA_2 line, so the EZO-EC circuit cannot be addressed or configured. Additionally, U8 actively drives I2C_SDA instead of operating as open-drain, which can cause bus contention when other devices pull the line low.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain an extra unidirectional buffer (U8, 74LVC1G34) inserted in the EC isolator's SDA path, breaking the bidirectional I2C connection to U4 and likely preventing communication with the EZO-EC circuit."
}

